I fixed #583 and committed it as be701451, but it hasn't landed on main yet. It has been in the land queue since 17:42Z and was still waiting when my time ran out. The manager will land it after this run, so the issue stays open and the next run finishes it.

**The fix**
- **Server:** the example server (`example/server/main.go`) now refuses to start unless `NOTES_ADDR` is a loopback address (`127.0.0.0/8`, `::1`) or `localhost`. It exits non-zero with a message that names loopback.
- **semgrep:** the `grpc.NewServer()` line has a `nosemgrep` comment saying it is loopback only and where that's enforced. semgrep flags the old file at line 161 and finds nothing in the new one.
- **Test:** `example/run.sh` (`just example`) now checks that `NOTES_ADDR=0.0.0.0:0` is refused before the end-to-end run. I ran it against the old server first and it failed, because the old server just served on 0.0.0.0. With the fix it passes and ends `==> example OK`.
- **Docs:** `example/README.md` and `README.md` (regenerated from `README.src.md`) now say the example is loopback only. `docs/USER.md` doesn't show the example, so I left it alone.
- **Follow-up:** I added an entry to `PROPOSALS.md`, because `just example` isn't in any gate set, so nothing would catch this check breaking later.

**Gates:** my local `just gates` ended `OVERALL fail=1`. Every gate passed except `current-generation`, and the only check that failed in it was the Java DiskStore timing test ("appends must not wait on a failing upload"). That's the known flaky test in #539, and the machine was busy running the land's queue next to my run. My diff touches no Java. The land's own run of the gates gives the real verdict.

**Release:** main has taken features since `v2.6.1`, so I didn't tag main. I opened backport pull requests for all seven release lines, each naming the patch tag to cut once it merges (or the next free one):

| Release line | PR | Tag |
|---|---|---|
| release/2.0 | #658 | `v2.0.31` |
| release/2.1 | #659 | `v2.1.24` |
| release/2.2 | #660 | `v2.2.21` |
| release/2.3 | #661 | `v2.3.23` |
| release/2.4 | #662 | `v2.4.23` |
| release/2.5 | #663 | `v2.5.24` |
| release/2.6 | #664 | `v2.6.12` |

`just example` passes on every line, including the new check, and the README-is-current test passes on 2.2 through 2.6. I didn't run the full gates on the release branches.

**Trace propagation:** the example server's three handlers make no outgoing calls. All 8 findings from `looper-trace check` are in the cross-test driver, which #311 already covers.

**Left for the next run:** get the land's verdict, put main's commit hash into the seven PR descriptions, post the final outcome comment and close #583. I posted a progress comment on the issue and saved a checkpoint that says the same.
